  "question": {
    "text": "A non-conducting rod of length <em>L</em>&nbsp;with linear charge density <math><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi></math> where <em>x</em> is the distance from end <em>A</em>&nbsp;is rotating with constant angular speed <math><mi>ω</mi></math> about the same end. If the angular velocity of the rod (<math><mi>ω</mi></math>) is large, then the magnetic dipole moment of the system is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>?<br />\r&nbsp;<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/bc0c8188-bc1f-4e56-8336-87597ad01a33-image15.jpeg\" />",
    "image": null
